{
  "$comment": "Navbar silo — the site's information architecture as a RECURSIVE tree. Editable content, safe for a CMS. Each node is { label, href?, icon?, desc?, comingSoon?, children? }: a node with `children` is a menu, a leaf has an `href`, and a node carrying BOTH is a menu you can also click (see Home) — on desktop it navigates on click and still opens its list on hover; on mobile it stays an accordion, which is why its own destination is repeated as the first child. The Navbar renders this to ANY depth (cascading flyouts on desktop, a nested single-open accordion on mobile), so adding a deeper sub-level needs no code change. `icon` is a KEY — a lucide-react component name resolved by NAV_ICONS in src/data/navIcons.js — because React components cannot be stored in JSON. HOME is the on-page menu: one row per section actually mounted by src/app/page.js, in page order, so every part of the home page is one click away. Those hrefs are element ids — if a section's id changes, change it here too. Every industry vertical carries the SAME EIGHT service pages (web, seo, automation, creative, content, facebook, google, social) with a `<vertical>-<service>` href pattern — keep that pattern when a new vertical is added so the flyout columns stay balanced.",
